# clangd 21.1.8 segfaults while parsing any file that includes
# data/ttavdata.h. Measured 2026-08-12: six of six diagnostic harnesses that
# include that header crash the language server (SIGSEGV in the parser, at a
# closing parenthesis inside a lambda body); no harness without it does. The
# crash is not a regression from the July upgrade - every affected file is
# younger than the installed clangd - and it could not be reduced to a small
# example in five attempts, so it needs the full translation unit rather than
# one construct.
#
# Index.Background: Skip only stops clangd's automatic background indexing
# of these files (the pass that used to crash repeatedly and leave a core
# dump behind on every project-wide (re)index). It does NOT prevent the
# crash if a file matching the pattern is opened and manually parsed in an
# editor - that still segfaults clangd. Consequence without this file:
# background indexing kills clangd, it restarts, dies again, and leaves a
# ~350 MB core dump behind each time (2.5 GB accumulated in fifteen minutes
# during the session that found it) - core dumps that `git status` does not
# show, because this repo sets status.showUntrackedFiles=no.
#
# The exclusion is deliberately narrow: tools/diag/ holds acceptance harnesses,
# not code anyone navigates daily. The application itself keeps full language
# support. Remove this block once upstream fixes the crash - the parser bug is
# in clangd, not in our code, and the compiler builds all of these files
# without complaint.
If:
  PathMatch: tools/diag/.*\.cpp

Index:
  Background: Skip
